All 15 tests pass. Here's a summary of the 8 bugs fixed across 3 files:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs)
1. `has_permission` — compared roles case-sensitively; now lowercases both sides before matching.
2. `is_admin_or_owner` — used `and` instead of `or`; admin status and owner status are independent grant conditions.

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
3. `__init__` — mutable default `{}` shared state across instances; replaced with `None` default + `dict(initial)` copy.
4. `add` — overwrote stock instead of accumulating; changed `self._stock[sku] = qty` to `+= qty`.
5. `reserve` — used `>=` so reserving exactly the available quantity raised `OutOfStock`; changed to `>`.
6. `release` — allowed reserved count to go negative; added a guard that raises `ValueError`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs)
7. `slugify` — didn't lowercase characters; now appends `char.lower()`.
8. `slugify` — single `replace("--", "-")` missed triple+ separators; replaced with a `while "--" in` loop.
9. `truncate` — `text[:max_len] + suffix` exceeded `max_len`; now slices to `max_len - len(suffix)`.
